--- DESCRIPTION ---
This patch replaces Vista+ threading APIs (SRWLOCK, CONDITION_VARIABLE)
with XP-compatible equivalents (CRITICAL_SECTION, Event objects).

Apply this to: ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c

Look for sections using SRWLOCK and CONDITION_VARIABLE and replace with:

--- FIND (approximate) ---

#ifdef _WIN32
typedef SRWLOCK ggml_lock_t;
#define ggml_lock_init(lock)    InitializeSRWLock(lock)
#define ggml_lock_lock(lock)    AcquireSRWLockExclusive(lock)
#define ggml_lock_unlock(lock)  ReleaseSRWLockExclusive(lock)
#define ggml_lock_destroy(lock)

--- REPLACE WITH ---

#ifdef _WIN32
typedef CRITICAL_SECTION ggml_lock_t;
#define ggml_lock_init(lock)    InitializeCriticalSection(lock)
#define ggml_lock_lock(lock)    EnterCriticalSection(lock)
#define ggml_lock_unlock(lock)  LeaveCriticalSection(lock)
#define ggml_lock_destroy(lock) DeleteCriticalSection(lock)

--- NOTES ---
The exact line numbers will vary by llama.cpp version.
The automated patch script (patch-for-xp.sh) handles this automatically.
If applying manually, search for "SRWLOCK" and "CONDITION_VARIABLE" in the
ggml source files and replace all occurrences.
